Mr. Boarden needs to cover two-thirds of a 36 square foot bathroom. First, calculate the area to be covered:  
\[
\frac{2}{3} \times 36 = 24 \text{ square feet}
\]  
Each square foot requires 24 tiles. Multiply the area by the number of tiles per square foot:  
\[
24 \text{ tiles/sq ft} \times 24 \text{ sq ft} = 576 \text{ tiles}
\]  

**Answer:** \boxed{576}

