To determine the total number of seashells brought back, we start by calculating the number of 9-person groups from 90 people:  
\[
\frac{90}{9} = 10 \text{ groups}
\]  
Next, we find the number of groups that had each member bring 2 seashells:  
\[
\frac{3}{5} \times 10 = 6 \text{ groups}
\]  
Each of these 6 groups contributed \(9 \text{ people} \times 2 \text{ seashells} = 18 \text{ seashells}\). Multiplying by the number of such groups gives:  
\[
6 \times 18 = 108 \text{ seashells}
\]  

\boxed{108}
